      "dataset_id": "nm000275",
      "id": "nm000275",
      "name": "Multi-channel EEG recordings during a sustained-attention driving task",
      "description": "This dataset comprises multi-channel EEG recordings from 27 healthy adults performing a sustained-attention driving task in a virtual-reality simulator across 62 sessions. The task involved event-related lane-departure paradigms where participants maintained vehicle position on a simulated highway, with recordings capturing 32-channel EEG (30 scalp + 2 mastoid references) sampled at 500 Hz alongside vehicle position data. The dataset includes approximately 82 hours of raw, unfiltered EEG data with over 27,000 lane-departure trials and associated behavioral markers, providing a resource for investigating fatigue, drowsiness, and sustained attention mechanisms.",
